r-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a Java program using synchronized threads, which demonstrates producer consumerconcept.</p><p data-ref="8a34d1b4-632f-40e8-9b1b-42e5c0d50416" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="3377c0eb-9ab6-4dc0-b6b4-db58f30e4aeb"></p><p data-ref="1af6f7b1-244a-4b47-8c88-4b45d06897ea" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The Producer-Consumer problem is a classic synchronization problem in computer science. It involves two types of threads:</p><ul data-ref="f98fc85e-5104-4578-96a7-a4d1a9cb9c6d" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="b77b127c-4b68-4e89-807b-cf10bcb3adf4"><strong data-ref="45664678-a591-40fc-b308-7a37da9d82b0">Producer</strong>: This thread generates data (e.g., items) and places it in a shared resource (like a buffer).</li><li data-ref="93085be1-4dbc-42db-bc88-64185d37df1d"><strong data-ref="e9a64d50-ed42-4500-8efc-66bf91b7202a">Consumer</strong>: This thread takes data (items) from the shared resource for processing or consumption.</li></ul><p data-ref="fabe3315-9f68-47b0-860d-16e1e2393e06" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="788b2ee2-051f-4a29-a04d-e2e899fcdc42"></p><p data-ref="c74c7738-61dd-4d4b-b868-3b9f3199c9cf" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The problem revolves around coordinating these threads such that:</p><ul data-ref="f422043f-b799-478e-a6ca-eef521dc750c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="46ff4a75-3b31-4760-baa4-2ce7d3bd01ee">The producer does not produce when the buffer is full.</li><li data-ref="c673efbb-f5f5-4c91-85de-67c481dd598d">The consumer does not consume when the buffer is empty.</li><li data-ref="af4f235b-cdb3-44e1-a4c7-d0cb71a7c6bb">Both threads operate safely without corrupting the shared resource.</li></ul><p data-ref="974591de-29cf-4d8d-a248-6885db2aedd3" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="2169ef2f-c62e-4f3c-97a1-238d2746c171"></p><p data-ref="a8491913-cecf-44f3-b0dc-9d7ebb56461e" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">To achieve synchronization in Java, we can use the synchronized keyword along with wait and notify methods to control the interaction between the threads.</p><p data-ref="eed499d3-a9af-442c-a98e-8753c51a959a" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="e67b8b00-1f89-47d6-8168-35151fbfb972"></p><p data-ref="6951e77a-b2d2-42b2-a687-878cf45a6964" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="87a49e74-ad6d-43da-ac00-dd7b6cb70579">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="25d22827-0bf0-4904-9805-39f55b4c4615" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="0042555c-a966-4fdf-8277-0aa217bea867">Prompt the user to enter an integer representing the number of items to produce along with a print statement <strong data-ref="89126756-2427-42a1-9d38-2c506dc7fc97">"Enter the number of items to produce: " </strong></li></ul><p data-ref="fcb32010-107f-47cd-9584-1a760bbb9735" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="06c2d17e-42e7-4cf4-9e77-b90bd8946aef"></p><p data-ref="ecf7ea35-6c68-41e9-b881-46f59ce7ed63" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="e3590ffb-436b-4851-9126-cf841c60f003">Output Format:</strong></p><p data-ref="4ccb4dec-20b0-4ed7-a0b8-0d0527377804" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Output should print the following:</p><ul data-ref="e0d11af9-6830-4f4a-b47e-5e709f04bb9c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="7b62fea2-e36b-4238-8711-0456fdf4ff91">Messages indicating the production of each item as &lt;Produced: {Produced item}&gt;</li><li data-ref="9e62270c-e97c-4405-8861-68fb4801fb08">Messages indicating the consumption of each item as &lt;Consumed: {Consumed item}&gt;</li></ul></span></div><div class="mb-3" data-ref="229ad8ac-3031-4de1-976e-786576256f28"><div class="ml-1 mb-3" data-ref="6ca633bc-e565-4884-9fed-88f3adfaeb85"><b style="border-bottom:1px solid black;" data-ref="54b391ac-9cea-450f-a141-4b760650b31a" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Source Code: </b></div><div class="user-solution" style="page-break-inside: auto" data-ref="cf49031c-7298-449a-85e7-3fc16e6467ba" data-undisplayed="undisplayed"><div class="px-3 pt-2 pb-1" style="font-family: monospace !important;border-radius: 4px 4px 0 0; border: 1px solid black; break-after: avoid; page-break-after: avoid;" data-ref="3d0fa32a-6b58-471a-8a6b-e8aa0fbe2b07" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">q28802/ProducerConsumerDemo.java</div> <pre style="overflow: visible; border: 1px solid black; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 4px;" class="px-3 pt-2 pb-1" data-ref="f3a8ff49-cfbf-4417-b326-6424b8cfc13d" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">package q28802;
import java.util.LinkedList;
import java.util.Scanner;
import java.util.LinkedList;
import java.util.Scanner;

class Buffer {
    private LinkedList&lt;Integer&gt; list = new LinkedList&lt;&gt;();
    private int capacity;

    // Constructor to initialize buffer capacity
    public Buffer(int capacity) {
        this.capacity = capacity;
    }

    public synchronized void produce(int item) throws InterruptedException {
        while (list.size() == capacity) {
            wait();
        }
        list.add(item);
        System.out.println("Produced: " + item);
        notify();
    }

    public synchronized int consume() throws InterruptedException {
        while (list.isEmpty()) {
            wait();
        }
        int item = list.removeFirst();
        System.out.println("Consumed: " + item);
        notify();
        return item;
    }
}

class Producer extends Thread {
    private Buffer buffer;
    private int itemCount;

    public Producer(Buffer buffer, int itemCount) {
        this.buffer = buffer;
        this.itemCount = itemCount;
    }

    public void run() {
        try {
            for (int i = 1; i &lt;= itemCount; i++) {
                buffer.produce(i);
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}

class Consumer extends Thread {
    private Buffer buffer;
    private int itemCount;

    public Consumer(Buffer buffer, int itemCount) {
        this.buffer = buffer;
        this.itemCount = itemCount;
    }

    public void run() {
        try {
            for (int i = 1; i &lt;= itemCount; i++) {
                buffer.consume();
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}



public class ProducerConsumerDemo {
	// Write your code here...
	public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter the number of items to produce: ");
        int n = sc.nextInt();

        Buffer buffer = new Buffer(n);
        Producer producer = new Producer(buffer, n);
        Consumer consumer = new Consumer(buffer, n);

        producer.start();
        consumer.start();
