d black;" data-ref="b06909a5-4a3c-4e13-96a6-439e8c276836" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="778c8ac3-9e5b-44f6-8f39-9131b2e731b9"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="5f7d79ac-997c-4228-91fe-d1ced43784d6"><p data-ref="b6c2f084-00b8-4c4b-8539-b3989032f264" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a Java program using synchronized threads, which demonstrates producer consumerconcept.</p><p data-ref="8a34d1b4-632f-40e8-9b1b-42e5c0d50416" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="3377c0eb-9ab6-4dc0-b6b4-db58f30e4aeb"></p><p data-ref="1af6f7b1-244a-4b47-8c88-4b45d06897ea" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The Producer-Consumer problem is a classic synchronization problem in computer science. It involves two types of threads:</p><ul data-ref="f98fc85e-5104-4578-96a7-a4d1a9cb9c6d" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="b77b127c-4b68-4e89-807b-cf10bcb3adf4"><strong data-ref="45664678-a591-40fc-b308-7a37da9d82b0">Producer</strong>: This thread generates data (e.g., items) and places it in a shared resource (like a buffer).</li><li data-ref="93085be1-4dbc-42db-bc88-64185d37df1d"><strong data-ref="e9a64d50-ed42-4500-8efc-66bf91b7202a">Consumer</strong>: This thread takes data (items) from the shared resource for processing or consumption.</li></ul><p data-ref="fabe3315-9f68-47b0-860d-16e1e2393e06" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="788b2ee2-051f-4a29-a04d-e2e899fcdc42"></p><p data-ref="c74c7738-61dd-4d4b-b868-3b9f3199c9cf" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The problem revolves around coordinating these threads such that:</p><ul data-ref="f422043f-b799-478e-a6ca-eef521dc750c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="46ff4a75-3b31-4760-baa4-2ce7d3bd01ee">The producer does not produce when the buffer is full.</li><li data-ref="c673efbb-f5f5-4c91-85de-67c481dd598d">The consumer does not consume when the buffer is empty.</li><li data-ref="af4f235b-cdb3-44e1-a4c7-d0cb71a7c6bb">Both threads operate safely without corrupting the shared resource.</li></ul><p data-ref="974591de-29cf-4d8d-a248-6885db2aedd3" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="2169ef2f-c62e-4f3c-97a1-238d2746c171"></p><p data-ref="a8491913-cecf-44f3-b0dc-9d7ebb56461e" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">To achieve synchronization in Java, we can use the synchronized keyword along with wait and notify methods to control the interaction between the threads.</p><p data-ref="eed499d3-a9af-442c-a98e-8753c51a959a" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="e67b8b00-1f89-47d6-8168-35151fbfb972"></p><p data-ref="6951e77a-b2d2-42b2-a687-878cf45a6964" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-lis