ata-ref="65ee4990-7f81-4636-8abe-32b8f1d674fb" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="19e9e45f-6add-4b90-8c2d-a3ef74afe0fe"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="d4562399-625d-41f7-bbeb-692926f3f163"><p data-ref="ce6bf2a5-9504-48fc-b4e0-c71978931ea6" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Create a Java program that demonstrates the use of user and daemon threads. Implement a class <strong data-ref="3265d846-302e-44e1-a838-0aeb9ac7c989">WorkerThread</strong> that extends <strong data-ref="f1601efa-b64e-4642-9434-794e332e2ba2">Thread</strong> and overrides the <strong data-ref="ad5f32a8-dba8-47b0-b61c-07118c3cb473">run</strong> method to simulate some work by printing messages and sleeping for a short duration.</p><p data-ref="f1501457-d998-47b7-b0eb-e25dfb4093c7" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="08cc38f8-ecbf-4730-a1b2-2393cfafd186"></p><p data-ref="06c374a8-2c71-47a5-91da-45789800331f" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">In the <strong data-ref="cd1bccfd-6e9b-41f1-bf40-bde692620256">DaemonThread</strong> class:</p><p data-ref="ce21fc63-6cae-4c7f-a7ad-5649afe453df" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">1. Prompt the user to input the number of user threads and daemon threads.</p><p data-ref="129a3eb0-7930-4498-a634-9995e552dfb9" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">2. Create and start the specified number of user threads and daemon threads.</p><ul data-ref="dfc2829d-85be-4f0a-bb72-058f1a58ffcb" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="ab59a1ba-6c54-4511-8ae1-5e77cec5d489"><strong data-ref="c6d487b6-cd8e-4649-8bc1-125c9bbfa8bd">User Threads: </strong>These threads will run to completion and are not interrupted by the main thread.<strong data-ref="302c008e-876d-4b29-9dda-0ca379f863fe">Daemon Threads:</strong> These threads will run in the background and may be terminated abruptly when the main thread exits.</li></ul><p data-ref="e520f4ff-2e4f-414a-92c4-1af764ce91ad" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">3. The main thread should print a message indicating its exit after creating the threads.</p><p data-ref="3c86ea92-5a6a-44a5-ae5d-dfa66b7487fa" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="cae30348-d24a-4979-b08a-d06a5293feb5"></p><p data-ref="5e14e25b-9b25-4578-973b-10be80a3fe93" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="1185db41-26ea-490f-a1e0-97307f9a201d">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="a482e088-0adf-4803-89b1-5821eec6992b" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="95825512-6ed2-4449-88ce-dc8bb4430e41">The first line contains an integer specifying the number of user threads.</li><li data-ref="3b0d8397-8f75-4683-b7df-ed92f6dfd294">The second line contains an integer specifying the number of daemon threads.</li></ul><p data-ref="f80a384a-b1c5-418b-8fef-ad63c797c523" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" da